# Working procedure (MEASURED 2026-10-19). All captures go through the T2443 replay queue.
# They use fast-forward (the default), Xvfb and lavapipe. Take a snapshot once at the
# gameplay-start poll. With `--snapshot-continue` the take run keeps running, and its trace in
# `<snapshot-dir>/continued` becomes the same-run oracle:
#
# ```sh
# SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)   # a commit with a published prebuilt (python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt build --commit "$SHA")
# ROUTE=../../routes/r10-story-level1-20261018-2030.rec
# DISC='../../owner/TimeSplitters - Future Perfect (USA) (XBOX).iso'
# SNAP=tmp/rust-trace/r10-gameplay-snapshot   # fresh path per take
# python3 -m tools.wt replay submit --route "$ROUTE" --switches off --commit "$SHA" --seconds 200 \
#   --max-dumps 5000 --regions tools/data/rust_trace_regions.json --headless --disc "$DISC" \
#   --host-arg=--vblank-poll-blank --host-arg=--vblank-owner-waits --host-arg=1000000 \
#   --host-arg=--vblank-worker-blanks --host-arg=1000000 \
#   --snapshot-at-poll 8816 --snapshot-dir "$SNAP" --snapshot-continue
# python3 -m tools.wt replay resume --snapshot-dir "$SNAP" --commit "$SHA"   # repeat as often as needed
# python3 -m tools.rust_trace diff --left "$PWD/$SNAP/continued" --right <resumed run_dir> \
#   --from-poll 8816 --strict-poll 20002 --min-samples 600 --report tmp/rust-trace/r10-resume-diff
# ```
#
# r10 enters in-level mode `0x2` at poll 8816. For r8, use `r8-arcade-20261018-2022.rec`
# with poll 24: the traced regions only vary before poll 100, and r8 stays in mode `0x65` up
# to its route end. Do not pass `--unlock-all`, because both recordings have it off. Pass the
# recording's own saves and settings, which are restored automatically. Use absolute paths for
# `diff --left`, since relative paths resolve into the shared data dir. Results: r10 had 2798
# samples, 15 regions non-empty and 15 varying, 0 diverging words, EQUAL. r8 had 4996 samples,
# 5 regions non-empty and 3 varying, EQUAL. The r10 take reaches poll 8816 in 83.4 s, and a
# resume restores in about 3 to 5 s, so each repeated r10 gameplay capture saves about 80 s.
# Details are in `docs/t2479-gameplay-snapshots.md`, "Working save and resume".
#
# Diagnostics: set `TSFP_SNAPSHOT_SEGV_REPORT=1` at take time. On restart, each process then
# logs its kernel break and glibc break, and on a crash it logs the fault address, RIP and
# `/proc/self/maps` to `<snapshot-dir>/resume-<port>.log`. Set `TSFP_SNAPSHOT_REAL_CLOCKS=1` at
# take time to turn off the restart clock-gap offset. `play.sh --replay` can still take or
# resume T1153 snapshots with `--snapshot-at-poll N --snapshot-dir DIR` or
# `--resume-snapshot DIR` after `--`.
#
# Adoption gate from gameplay start: add `--snapshot-poll 8832` to
# `python3 -m tools.adoption_gate --route ../../routes/r10-story-level1-20261018-2030.rec
# --switches <set> --commit <sha>`, with the r10 `--host-arg` values above. The first run takes and
# caches one snapshot per switch set. Reruns resume them, about 137 s against about 219 s for a
# full gate. `--headless --from-poll 8832` runs the full-replay gate on the same window. Do not
# start two gates at once that need the same uncached snapshot.
