# Headless fast-forward `.rec` replays deliver vblanks from guest virtual time even when the host receives `--interactive --no-vblank-poll-blank --no-vblank-worker-blanks`. Submit captures through `python3 -m tools.wt replay submit --priority high`; keep `TSFP_RUST_FRAME_LOOP=0` and `TSFP_RUST_STARTUP_VBLANK_CLOCK=1` for the T3580 control. Diff captures with `python3 -m tools.rust_trace diff`. Use `sh tools/dev/play.sh [variant]` for owner-facing live play.
#
# `sh tools/dev/play.sh --emit-options [--replay f.rec] [variant]` prints the variant's host environment and arguments as JSON and exits (no host lookup); `tools.rust_trace capture` and the replay queue read it, so they run what a live `play.sh` runs.
#
# T3597 changes no play command. The prebuilt that `sh tools/dev/play.sh` selects now contains the
# allocator modules, selected only by `TSFP_RUST_GAME_*` (unset keeps the lifted C).
#
# Replay captures now preserve the default `TSFP_RUST_KMEM=1` setting. Tier 2 controls must use `python3 -m tools.gate --profile weapons --route story-level1 --no-cache`, which submits captures through the shared replay queue.
#
# No runtime behavior or replay inputs change. Cache hits restore the same keyed build artifacts and validate the lift receipt or prebuilt manifest before selection.
#
# T3608 does not change gameplay selection; `sh tools/dev/play.sh default` remains the owner live check.
#
# Play and replay commands are unchanged. The LTO-off candidate reached route end, but the controlled weapons gate diverged from baseline at poll 5151; do not adopt the option until the state difference is explained and equivalence is established. Reproduce route completion with `python3 -m tools.regress run --sha <candidate> --route story-hud-weapons --no-block` and state comparison with `python3 -m tools.gate --profile weapons --route story-hud-weapons --start gameplay`.
#
# No runtime setting changes. The T3612 comparison uses the same original function bodies and registration receipt; no replay capture is required for this generated-source-only split.
#
# Guest-frame timing, scheduler and draw-assembly subphase diagnostics are observational host data. They do not write guest state or change the fixed 60 Hz simulation. `--no-guest-frame-trace` disables the trace and scheduler sampling. `--t3615-draw-phase-timing` separately enables draw-subphase sampling; it is off by default and uses the guest thread CPU clock.
#
# Shadow mode executes the selected Rust lane and its lifted C original against the same entry register/stack and watched guest regions. The lifted result remains authoritative. The first mismatch is written to the configured shadow log with root, poll, call ordinal, arguments, register/stack differences and first differing byte per watched region. On shutdown, `SHADOW_SUMMARY` reports the number of completed comparisons and whether a mismatch was found, including when all comparisons match.
#
# 2026-10-23 measurements: memory-arena root `0x237480` shadowed 1 call EQUAL in 221.47 s; the existing gate's 24 h median was 106.3 s. The arcade-weapon-reload gate took 533.83 s but was VACUOUS, and its 10.461 s shadow replay compared 0 calls. The weapons result is not behavioural evidence; its route must be fixed to exercise `0x1B7BC0` before measuring that root.
#
# No runtime behavior or replay input changes.
#
# No runtime behavior or replay inputs change. The same C2R roots remain selected through the `tsfp-ports::c2r` re-exports.
#
# T3680: play variants are unchanged; `tools.gate` and standalone `tools.rust_trace` inherit the same pinned Rust environment before launching build or trace work.
#
# `sh tools/dev/play.sh` picks the host in this order: `TSFP_HOST`, the binary in `tmp/play/last-build.json`, `$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/tsfp-bevy`, then the prebuilt cache and `tmp/bevy-target` default. It prints which host it chose and why (`--print-host` prints only that). `--hotkey` without `--hotkey-dir` now writes `hotkey.<n>` under `<run-dir>/hotkeys`.
#
# Capture replay of an owner recording, headless and fast-forward: `python3 -m tools.wt replay submit --route <rec> --switches off --commit <sha> --t2-capture-host <capture host tsfp-bevy>`, or `python3 -m tools.rust_trace capture --t2-capture --host <capture host> ...`. The spool is written as gzip segments `<run dir>/capture.bin.seg-NNNNNN.gz` that the run ingests into the corpus and deletes while it plays (T3745), with `capture.bin.stats.json` and `capture.bin.compact.json`; a leftover segment is ingested with `python3 -m tools.t2corpus ingest <run dir>/capture.bin`. Disk limits: `docs/t3745-disk-safety.md`.
#
# T3745 disk safety: `sh tools/dev/play.sh` exports `TMPDIR` on the data disk and runs `python3 -m tools.datadisk check --kind play` first (exit 3 with the reason when over budget or under a free floor). A rule-43 capture never writes to the root disk, stops cleanly at 4 GB per run or at the 60 GB free floor (the game keeps running, the stats say `truncated`), and its spool stays bounded: gzip segments of 256 MB are ingested into the corpus and deleted while the game runs. Check with `python3 -m tools.datadisk status`; limits and tuning in `docs/t3745-disk-safety.md`.
#
# Recapture with the current runtime: `python3 -m tools.t2capture.recapture --host <capture tsfp-bevy> --commit <sha> --hosts laptop --only <stem,...>`. A recording already in the store from an older capture runtime is captured again and its older entries are superseded (`tools/t2corpus/store.py`, per-entry `capture_version`).
#
# T3771 two players: with the input router (default variant) every connected controller is its own guest controller: the first pad shares player 1 with the mouse and keyboard, the second pad is player 2 (guest port 1), up to four. The shell adds the host flag `--pad-ports` itself; `TSFP_PAD_PORTS=0 sh tools/dev/play.sh` returns to the old single pad behaviour. The log says `tsfp-bevy: guest pad port 1 connected (router slot 1, T3771)` when the second pad joins.
#
# No play change. A capture replay from a T3794 capture host records entries for functions that had none (0x9A4C0, the HUD draws); see docs/t3738-capture-design.md "T3794 results".
#
# No play change.
#
# T3812: quit the game window with **Alt+F4** (or the window close button). Ctrl+Q no longer quits: Ctrl is crouch and Q is melee, so the old chord closed the game during play. Neither Alt nor F4 is bound in the game.
#
# T3820: `--record` now writes input.rec format v6: every key, mouse, cursor, focus and pad event is stored at the single device intake before any page or the router sees it (`D` rows, plus the build id in the header), so native pages (profiles, players, storage names, text fields, Map Maker text, options binding capture, keyboard and mouse on original pages) replay the way you played. `--replay` of a v6 file feeds the recorded devices to every page and ignores live devices except Alt+F4 (the recording's own Alt+F4 is not replayed); the raw-look guard and slot-owner decisions are replayed as recorded, and the stop line reports `device rows delivered=... decisions applied=... routes checked=... mismatched=...`. Files recorded before this build (v5 and older) replay as before and print a WARN that native-page input is missing: re-record the routes that use front-end, profile, two-player or Map Maker pages.
#
# T3824: every run writes `tmp/play/<run>/census-hits.bin` and keeps a copy in `tmp/live-census/` (the host prints `live census: N of M lifted functions ran`). Nothing changes for you; just play normally. `python3 -m tools.live_census runs` lists your sessions.
#
# T3833: `sh tools/dev/play.sh --capture-targets` (or `--capture-targets auto`, or `--capture-targets FILE` with one hex VA per line) plays the normal game, but on a capture host that records Tier 2 corpus entries for a few thousand not-yet-covered functions only. The first run per commit builds that host (several minutes). At exit the record goes to `tmp/play/<run>/capture.bin` and is added to the corpus (`capture targets: ingested ...`). It is opt-in because it has no measured bound under 5% yet (deck CPU A/B inconclusive). Play anything you like; menus, Map Maker and story levels are the most useful.
#
# T3844: play is unchanged.
#
# Play with `sh tools/dev/play.sh [variant]`.
# Normal play can reuse a cached host for the current committed task branch. Uncommitted host-source changes still use a local build; owner runs do not publish into the shared prebuilt cache.
# With `--capture-targets`, the capture host uses the shared variant cache and the configured remote build policy. Existing hosts in the older capture cache are reused before building; explicit capture-cache and remote overrides remain available.
#
# Play with `sh tools/dev/play.sh [variant]`. The Rust XInput dispatch and enumeration path is the default; set `TSFP_RUST_INPUT_HLE=0` for the C fallback (kept for one release).
#
# For the experimental Rust file-I/O mount sequence, also set `TSFP_RUST_FILEIO_HOST_SETUP=1`; it refuses `--legacy-fileio`. No C runtime has been retired.
#
# `sh tools/dev/play.sh --renderer native [variant]` opts into the UNVERIFIED T3887 DrawList preview. Captured vertex/index payload bounds and index ranges are checked before constructing and validating a `tsfp-scene-model` DrawList; the preview overlays placeholder geometry through `tsfp-render-preview`. The default renderer remains unchanged and the preview is not parity evidence.
#
# No play change.
#
# No play change: `TSFP_RUST_KMEM=1` was already the default and is now the only mode.
#
# The host no longer accepts `--legacy-fileio`. The layer-2 C implementation
# has been retired; all current play variants use native Rust file I/O. Archived
# pre-removal gate receipts and their C-oracle identity remain historical evidence.
#
# The runtime-mapped wave 3 roots are included in the opt-in `all` set but remain excluded from the default play variant through `blocked_roots` until shadow-live evidence is clean and the smoke suite passes. An explicit per-VA `--rust-ports=0x...` selection remains available for shadow runs. `0xC1850` and `0xC15B0` are not currently in the runtime root map. The known divergent root `0x153270` remains excluded.
# <!-- run-notes:play end -->
# Paths are relative to the repository root, resolved from this script's own location.
# CPU diagnostics: tools.t2333_trace retains dummy SDL PCM consumption without a GPU.
#!/bin/sh
. "$(dirname "$0")/renderer-selection.sh"



#
# VARIANT TABLE: the single place to update. Each variant sets ENVV (env assignments) and ARGS (tools.play arguments) and
# has a status label. Keep docs/owner-run-guide.md in step. Statuses: RECOMMENDED, RECOMMENDED-CANDIDATE, EXPERIMENTAL, DIAGNOSTIC.
set -eu

# Base arguments of the recommended smooth configuration (T2143 measurements, docs/t-perf-playtest.md).
# Owner crash 2026-10-13: entering Map Maker calls XOnlineStartup; Xbox Live is drop class (rule 14), so every variant runs the offline XONLINE policy.
BASE="--window --interactive --gpu-live --gpu-live-inferred --pad-source gamepad --xonline-offline"

variant_list() {
    # name|status|what it is for
    cat <<'LIST'
default|RECOMMENDED|shared GPU texture presentation (T2229, no CPU readback; -- --wgpu-live=cpu for evidence) + T2242 native UI/HUD animation at display rate (TSFP_UI_DISPLAY_RATE=0 = original guest-rate presentation) + T2168 owner decision 2026-10-13: legacy + keyboard and mouse (the mk player) + the Rust UI main menu + T2238 native T2334 object transform history producer (Tier 2 selected outputs on Arcade and Story; TSFP_NATIVE_OBJECT_TRANSFORM=0 restores original, full ScenePair acceptance remains open). Main menu: drawn by Rust, mouse hover/click, right click or Esc = Back, arrows/Enter, pad D-pad/A/B, pointer free; all UI pages: Enter selects, Esc backs, Space never selects; gameplay: the mk keys (Esc = Start), raw mouse look, pointer captured (Ctrl+Alt or F10 releases), a pad takes over when used; F9 hands the main menu back to the original input
legacy|RECOMMENDED|the previous default, pad only and original menus: ports all + Rust kernel memory/file I/O + wgpu live + readback ring + fast hooks, the window shows the wgpu picture (--wgpu-live, T2295); TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=0 avoids hook timers (T2255); comparison and fallback: sh tools/dev/play.sh legacy
plain|RECOMMENDED|previous default: ports all + Rust kernel memory/file I/O, C Vulkan live renderer; fallback: sh tools/dev/play.sh plain
safe|RECOMMENDED|--rust-ports=off, all game code from the lifted C (the comparison baseline)
rust|RECOMMENDED|alias of plain (previous default)
fileio|RECOMMENDED|ports all plus --rust-fileio (Rust disc/FATX, host descriptors, metadata/streams, resolution/create/rename, volume/cache orchestration, device mount validation/acquisition/publication, metadata conversion, guest OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES and bounded root-path adapters and attempt/observer state; T2225 extensions Tier 1 synthetic); Tier 2 Story route EQUAL 145/145 (T2111); owner play fine
kio|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus TSFP_RUST_KIO=1 (Rust NT I/O, async completion and file objects; Tier 1 synthetic, Tier 2 pending)
rtl|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus TSFP_RUST_RTL=all (pure Rust kernel RTL; Tier 1 C-host evidence only)
kclock|RECOMMENDED|default with TSFP_RUST_KCLOCK=1 spelled out: the Rust elapsed clock is already the default (T2207, Tier 2 EQUAL Story and Map Maker, frame-rate mutant diverges); TSFP_RUST_KCLOCK=0 sh tools/dev/play.sh selects the C clock
kmem|RECOMMENDED|ports all plus TSFP_RUST_KMEM=1 (Rust kernel memory); Tier 2 EQUAL on 5 routes, fault mutant diverges (T2048); owner play fine
wgpu|RECOMMENDED|alias of legacy (wgpu readback ring, pad only); TSFP_WGPU_SCALE=2 opts into 2x
wgpu-ring|RECOMMENDED|explicit alias of legacy with the T2227 nonblocking readback ring
wgpu-sync|DIAGNOSTIC|default configuration with synchronous CPU readback; A/B fallback for the ring
wgpu-hfr|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus the T2279/T2281/T2287/T2292 high framerate opt-ins (TSFP_RENDER_RATE_EXTRA=1 with the T2273 palette rebuild, TSFP_RENDER_RATE_ADAPT=2 replay shedding, TSFP_RENDER_RATE_DECOUPLE=1, TSFP_RENDER_RATE_STEP=wall 59.94 Hz pacing, TSFP_LIVE_FRAME_OFFPATH=drop): about 123 presents/s at 59.94 ticks/s on llvmpipe (Tier 0); audio may be choppy (T2279 dropped 4.3M frames under DECOUPLE), fallback: sh tools/dev/play.sh
wgpu-stats|DIAGNOSTIC|default plus TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=1 (hook timers enabled)
ui-display|EXPERIMENTAL|native Rust UI page/HUD fades, pulses, message slides and radar sweep on the shared GPU, recomposed each display update; reticles keep guest cadence, original default unchanged
wgpu-share|EXPERIMENTAL|wgpu plus --wgpu-share (T2229/T2246): the shell shares one Vulkan device with Bevy and the render runtime (linked into the shell, one wgpu copy), the renderer frame reaches the window as a GPU texture with no CPU readback; ONE startup line says path=gpu-texture or path=cpu-readback and why; needs sh tools/dev/build.sh rebuilt after T2246 (an older shell hangs or refuses); RADV headless: no stall at 1280x960 to 2880x2160, 0.14-0.18 ms shell blit per frame; RADV Bevy window qualified (T2229, private compatible build; release performance remains unmeasured)
perf|DIAGNOSTIC|default plus TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=1 --perf-log, stderr in tmp/perf-<variant>-<time>.err, tells you what to send back
bisect GROUPS|DIAGNOSTIC|default with --rust-ports=all,-GROUPS, e.g. bisect char,physics (groups: char physics npc inventory cutscene save audio render hud pose settings)
widescreen|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus --aspect 16:9 (the game's own 16:9 mode)
ultrawide|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus --aspect 21:9 (game renders 21:9 Hor+ via --aspect-override, T2094; HUD stays 4:3 laid out)
superwide|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus --aspect 32:9 (as ultrawide, horizontal FOV about 123 degrees)
mk|EXPERIMENTAL|legacy plus --rust-ports=all,player (the raw look hook lives in the player roots, T2200) --input-router --mouse-keyboard --raw-look (T2160, T2161 raw mouse look, Auto Aim/Lookahead/Inverse Look off for that player): player 1 on mouse and keyboard (T2179 keys: WASD move, mouse aim, LMB fire, RMB aim/zoom, MMB weapon alt mode, wheel next/previous weapon, 1-9 weapon slot, R reload, Esc pause, F melee, G grenade, Space jump, Ctrl or C crouch, E use), pointer captured, Ctrl+Alt or F10 releases it; a pad takes over when used; extra args after -- : --input-preset NAME[:slot] (original default, modern, mouse-raw, T2167)
mk-interim|EXPERIMENTAL|as mk but --no-raw-look: the mouse look is the interim virtual right stick through the original shaper (T2160), assists as in the profile
storage-import|DIAGNOSTIC|migrate existing HDD-directory or FATX-partition saves into the one PC storage; use storage-import -- SOURCE [--offset BYTES --length BYTES]; existing saves never overwritten, conflicts exit 3
ui-rust|EXPERIMENTAL|NOT the game: draws the main menu page with the Rust UI (--ui=rust, PagePresenter on wgpu, software adapter) from your captured menu tree tmp/ui-tree/tree.json into tmp/ui-preview/main-menu.ppm (and .png); row text from your disc (original font, its per-letter widths and strings, T2189 slice 16), legacy fallback (exit 4) when the layout is incomplete; extra args after -- go to tsfp-ui-preview (--ui=legacy, --page 0xID, --size WxH, --lang e|f|g|i|s)
ui-rust-shell|EXPERIMENTAL|legacy plus the interactive Rust UI main menu (T2188) without the mk player: arrows/Enter/Esc, mouse hover and click, pad D-pad/A/B move its focus and select through the original handlers; other pages stay legacy and the overlay hides there; F9 hands the menu back to the original input
all-rust|EXPERIMENTAL|default plus TSFP_RUST_RTL=all TSFP_RUST_KIO=1 TSFP_RUST_KCLOCK=1; RTL and NT I/O Tier 2 pending
LIST
}

usage() {
    cat <<'USAGE'
usage: sh tools/dev/play.sh [--renderer original|native] [--dry-run] [--allow-stale] [--timeout SECONDS] [--record | --replay FILE] [--replay-hold] [--unlock-all] [variant [GROUPS]] [-- extra tools.play args]

Runs python3 -m tools.play with the Bevy binary and the disc. Environment (optional):
  TSFP_FRAME_BUDGET      1 logs steady-state window/handoff CPU costs and submission rate on exit
  TSFP_SHARED_BLIT_CACHE  0 restores uncached shared-blit bindings for performance A/B (default cached)
  TSFP_PRESENT_MODE      vsync prefers Mailbox (Fifo fallback); fifo is blocking VSync; default uncapped
  TSFP_RUST_KSERVICES     explicit K-3 ordinal list for guarded Rust (default off; experimental)
  TSFP_KSERVICES_COMPARE  explicit K-3 ordinal list for C-oracle comparison (default off)
  TSFP_WGPU_BATCH_UPLOADS / TSFP_WGPU_PERSISTENT_PRESENT  1 enables experimental caches (default off)
  TSFP_WGPU_VSH_MIN_VERTICES  GPU threshold sweep (default 24, minimum 5; tuning pending)
  Renderer backlog preserves retained surface writes; drop-behind arguments no longer omit draws
  TSFP_DISC   disc image (default: tmp/TimeSplitters - Future Perfect (USA) (XBOX).iso)
  TSFP_HOST   host binary (default: the binary tmp/play/last-build.json records, then $CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/tsfp-bevy, then tmp/bevy-target/release/tsfp-bevy; in agent worktrees the shared prebuilt for the primary merge-base first)
  TSFP_UI_COMPOSE  overlay = Rust UI main menu as the old overlay picture (debug A/B, T2313); default: inside the game frame (T2309)
  --record   write native gameplay inputs to tmp/play/<variant>-<time>/input.rec; press F12 to add a mark
  --renderer original|native  select default rendering or the UNVERIFIED T3887 DrawList preview (default original)
  --replay FILE  replay typed gameplay inputs and recorded Rust main-menu UiInput events from an input.rec
  --replay-hold  preserve late events and keep simulating with neutral input after replay (requires --replay)
  --unlock-all  set the game's own unlock override at boot (TEMPORARY-SHIM; default off)
  --lifted-effects  A/B for the Story white/cyan blob glitch (T3502): the lifted C serves the effect and particle roots (the `effects` port group, derived from tsfp-engine-render effect, effect_setup, emitter, particle and the effects live-return crate), every other port stays as the variant says; no effect on safe/fileio
  --capture-targets [auto|FILE]  live targeted capture (T3833): a capture play host records only the ALLOW list VAs (auto = corpus gaps) to tmp/play/<run>/capture.bin and ingests it into tmp/t2corpus-f2; the rest of the game runs as usual
  --timeout SECONDS  hard-kill the play runner after this many seconds (runner option, not a host argument)
  --show-fps  extra argument after --: native top-right game fps / present fps (original font, off by default; wgpu variants)
  TSFP_SHOW_FPS  1 enables the same counter; e.g. sh tools/dev/play.sh default -- --show-fps
  --print-host  print the host binary play.sh would run and why (stderr), then exit
  --dry-run   print the command and the environment, do not run it
  --emit-options  print the variant's host environment and arguments as JSON (T3592: the one source tools.rust_trace capture, gates and replay queue read), no host lookup, do not run
  --allow-stale  run even if the binary is older than the sources (or TSFP_ALLOW_STALE=1)
  TSFP_STORAGE_TOOL  native migration tool (default: $CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/tsfp-storage, or tmp/bevy-target/release/tsfp-storage)
  --save-dir DIR    extra tools.play diagnostic override for isolated storage
  TSFP_BUILD_STAMP  stamp file (default: next to the host binary, .tsfp-build-stamp)

Opt-in switches (all default off; each is an A/B against the normal route):
  TSFP_NATIVE_RENDER_PREP=1  audit the native bounded room plan without D3D payload capture; =2 also submits sampled supported packets through wgpu (comparison layer)
  TSFP_RUST_FRAME_LOOP=1     Rust fixed-60 frame scheduler and 75-slot callback timer owner (T1670)
  TSFP_REA_INVENTORY_NATIVE=1  native REA interaction and inventory lookup route (T2377)
  TSFP_UI_MAPMAKER_HISTORY=1   Rust Map Maker undo/redo history (T2383)
  -- --rust-weapon-hands     typed Rust reload/unload/holster/equip hand-state adapters (T2376; needs a TSFP_RUST_PORTS build)
  -- --rust-rea-ai           Rust REA AI adoption: scorer, awareness, XZ approach, route advance, mechanism ticks (T2385)
  -- --story-progress-rust   typed Rust Story mission outcome saved through the selected profile (T2369)
  --record / --replay FILE / --unlock-all  see the option list above
  TSFP_BUILD_TIMEOUT=SECONDS  for build.sh: whole-build time limit (default 300, 1200 for relift/clean; 0 disables)

Keys in the window: Esc = pause menu (the pad START; press again to close), Alt+F4 or the window close button quits (Ctrl+Q no longer quits, T3812).

Variants (status):
USAGE
    variant_list | while IFS='|' read -r vname vstatus vdesc; do
        printf '  %-14s %-22s %s\n' "$vname" "$vstatus" "$vdesc"
    done
}

dry=0
print_host=0
emit_options=0
renderer=original
variant=""
groups=""
record=0
replay=""
replay_hold=0
unlock_all=0
lifted_effects=0
capture_targets=""
play_timeout=""
allow_stale=${TSFP_ALLOW_STALE:-0}
while :; do
    case ${1:-} in
    --renderer) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --renderer needs original or native" >&2; exit 2; }; renderer=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --renderer=*) renderer=${1#--renderer=}; shift ;;
    --dry-run) dry=1; shift ;;
    --print-host) dry=1; print_host=1; shift ;;
    --emit-options) dry=1; emit_options=1; shift ;;
    --allow-stale) allow_stale=1; shift ;;
    --record) record=1; shift ;;
    --replay) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --replay needs a file" >&2; exit 2; }; replay=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --replay-hold) replay_hold=1; shift ;;
    --unlock-all) unlock_all=1; shift ;;
    --lifted-effects) lifted_effects=1; shift ;;
    --capture-targets) shift; if [ "${1:-}" = auto ] || { [ -n "${1:-}" ] && [ -f "$1" ]; }; then capture_targets=$1; shift; else capture_targets=auto; fi ;;
    --capture-targets=*) capture_targets=${1#--capture-targets=}; shift ;;
    --timeout) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --timeout needs seconds" >&2; exit 2; }; play_timeout="--timeout $2"; shift 2 ;;
    *) break ;;
    esac
done
case ${1:-} in
--help | -h) usage; exit 0 ;;
--) ;;
'') ;;
-*) echo "play.sh: unknown option $1 (see --help)" >&2; exit 2 ;;
*) variant=$1; shift ;;
esac
[ -n "$variant" ] || variant=default
if [ "$variant" = bisect ]; then
    [ $# -ge 1 ] && [ "$1" != -- ] || { echo "play.sh: bisect needs GROUPS, e.g. play.sh bisect char,physics" >&2; exit 2; }
    groups=$1
    shift
fi
while :; do
    case ${1:-} in
    --renderer) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --renderer needs original or native" >&2; exit 2; }; renderer=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --renderer=*) renderer=${1#--renderer=}; shift ;;
    --dry-run) dry=1; shift ;;
    --print-host) dry=1; print_host=1; shift ;;
    --emit-options) dry=1; emit_options=1; shift ;;
    --allow-stale) allow_stale=1; shift ;;
    --record) record=1; shift ;;
    --replay) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --replay needs a file" >&2; exit 2; }; replay=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --replay-hold) replay_hold=1; shift ;;
    --unlock-all) unlock_all=1; shift ;;
    --lifted-effects) lifted_effects=1; shift ;;
    --capture-targets) shift; if [ "${1:-}" = auto ] || { [ -n "${1:-}" ] && [ -f "$1" ]; }; then capture_targets=$1; shift; else capture_targets=auto; fi ;;
    --capture-targets=*) capture_targets=${1#--capture-targets=}; shift ;;
    --timeout) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "play.sh: --timeout needs seconds" >&2; exit 2; }; play_timeout="--timeout $2"; shift 2 ;;
    *) break ;;
    esac
done
[ "${1:-}" != -- ] || shift
extra="$*"
[ "$replay_hold" = 0 ] || [ -n "$replay" ] || { echo "play.sh: --replay-hold requires --replay" >&2; exit 2; }
[ "$record" = 0 ] || [ -z "$replay" ] || { echo "play.sh: --record and --replay cannot be used together" >&2; exit 2; }

# T2319: migration is a native filesystem operation, before any game/window setup.
# T2424: default disc, found in this tree, then the main checkout (common dir) and its
# tmp/owner. Harness worktrees have no disc of their own. TSFP_DISC still wins.
default_disc() {
    top=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
    PYTHONPATH="$top${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}" python3 -m tools.owner_files disc --root "$top"
}

if [ "$variant" = storage-import ]; then
    [ "$record" = 0 ] && [ -z "$replay" ] || { echo "play.sh: --record/--replay need a game variant" >&2; exit 2; }
    root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
    cd "$root"
    target_dir=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-tmp/bevy-target}
    storage_tool=${TSFP_STORAGE_TOOL:-$target_dir/release/tsfp-storage}
    if [ "$dry" = 1 ]; then
        printf '%s migrate' "$storage_tool"
        for arg in "$@"; do printf ' [%s]' "$arg"; done
        printf '\n'
        exit 0
    fi
    [ -x "$storage_tool" ] || { echo "play.sh: no $storage_tool; run: sh tools/dev/build.sh --with-tools" >&2; exit 3; }
    exec "$storage_tool" migrate "$@"
fi

# T2189 slice 14: ui-rust is not a host run, it renders the Rust UI main menu offscreen and stops.
if [ "$variant" = ui-rust ]; then
    [ "$record" = 0 ] && [ -z "$replay" ] || { echo "play.sh: --record/--replay need a game variant" >&2; exit 2; }
    root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
    cd "$root"
    target_dir=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-tmp/bevy-target}
    preview=${TSFP_UI_PREVIEW:-$target_dir/release/tsfp-ui-preview}
    tree=${TSFP_UI_TREE:-tmp/ui-tree/tree.json}
    out=tmp/ui-preview/main-menu.ppm
    disc=${TSFP_DISC:-$(default_disc)}
    if [ "$dry" = 1 ]; then echo "$preview --ui=rust --tree $tree --disc '$disc' --out $out $extra"; exit 0; fi
    [ -x "$preview" ] || { echo "play.sh: no $preview, run: sh tools/dev/build.sh --with-tools" >&2; exit 3; }
    [ -e "$tree" ] || { echo "play.sh: no menu tree at $tree (set TSFP_UI_TREE), see docs/owner-run-guide.md" >&2; exit 4; }
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    if [ -e "$disc" ]; then set -- --disc "$disc"; else echo "play.sh: no disc at '$disc' (set TSFP_DISC), panels only" >&2; set --; fi
    status=0; "$preview" --ui=rust --tree "$tree" "$@" --out "$out" $extra || status=$?
    if [ "$status" = 0 ] && command -v convert >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        convert "$out" tmp/ui-preview/main-menu.png && echo "play.sh: open tmp/ui-preview/main-menu.png"
    fi
    exit "$status"
fi

# --- the variant table proper ---
# T3398 PLAYTEST BLOCKER MITIGATION (rule 25, docs/run-notes/T3398.md): root 0x153270 (objchar_wired4 matrix multiply) faults in Map Maker preview; lifted C serves it until fixed.
blocked_roots="-0x153270,-0x153B40,-0x9B090,-0x4A210,-0x9B800,-0x277FE0,-0xA64D0,-0xA6290,-0x247A0,-0x2FC470,-0x2F8140,-0x16FC00,-0x91EC0,-0x57040,-0x1CEBA0,-0x9A060,-0xD9030,-0x16CA00,-0x3FAA0,-0xdc110,-0xdb4c0,-0xc45f0,-0x166260,-0x158cb0,-0x12e90,-0x2db010,-0xb1f50,-0x744f0,-0x9b200,-0x98380,-0x154f30,-0x715e0,-0x99c00,-0x3462a0,-0x9b900,-0xc4350,-0xa4330,-0xc54a0,-0x76150,-0xa3ae0"
ports="--rust-ports=all,$blocked_roots"
perf=0
# T2229: default = shared GPU textures; T2227 readback ring remains the CPU control.
# File I/O is native Rust in every play variant; there is no C selector after retirement.
PLAIN_ENV="TSFP_RUST_KMEM=1"
WGPU_ENV="$PLAIN_ENV TSFP_WGPU_LIVE=1 TSFP_WGPU_PIPELINED_READBACK=1 TSFP_RT_HOST_FAST_HOOKS=1"
ENVV="$WGPU_ENV TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=0"
ARGS="--rust-fileio"
# T2168: the mk player (T2160/T2161/T2179/T2200); the default combines it with the Rust UI front end.
MK_ARGS="--input-router --mouse-keyboard --raw-look"
case $variant in
default) if [ "$record" = 1 ] || [ -n "$replay" ]; then simulation_pace=1; else simulation_pace=${TSFP_SIMULATION_PACE:-1}; fi; ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_SIMULATION_PACE=$simulation_pace TSFP_UI_DISPLAY_RATE=${TSFP_UI_DISPLAY_RATE:-1} TSFP_NATIVE_OBJECT_TRANSFORM=${TSFP_NATIVE_OBJECT_TRANSFORM:-1}"; [ "$simulation_pace" = 0 ] || ARGS="$ARGS --present-no-pace"; ports="--rust-ports=all,player,$blocked_roots"; ARGS="$ARGS --wgpu-share $MK_ARGS"; ui_overlay=1 ;;
legacy) ;;
rust) ENVV="$PLAIN_ENV"; echo "play.sh: note: rust is an alias of plain (previous default)" >&2 ;;
plain) ENVV="$PLAIN_ENV" ;;
safe) ports="--rust-ports=off"; ENVV="" ;;
fileio) ENVV=""; ARGS="--rust-fileio" ;;
rtl) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_RUST_RTL=all" ;;
kclock) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_RUST_KCLOCK=1" ;;
kmem) ENVV="TSFP_RUST_KMEM=1" ;;
wgpu) echo "play.sh: note: wgpu is an alias of legacy (readback ring, pad only)" >&2 ;;
wgpu-ring) echo "play.sh: note: wgpu-ring is an alias of legacy" >&2 ;;
wgpu-sync) ENVV="$PLAIN_ENV TSFP_WGPU_LIVE=1 TSFP_WGPU_PIPELINED_READBACK=0 TSFP_RT_HOST_FAST_HOOKS=1 TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=0" ;;
wgpu-hfr) ARGS="$ARGS --present-no-pace"; ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_RENDER_RATE_EXTRA=${TSFP_RENDER_RATE_EXTRA:-1} TSFP_RENDER_RATE_ADAPT=2 TSFP_RENDER_RATE_DECOUPLE=1 TSFP_RENDER_RATE_STEP=wall TSFP_LIVE_FRAME_OFFPATH=drop TSFP_BEVY_UNFOCUSED_CONTINUOUS=${TSFP_BEVY_UNFOCUSED_CONTINUOUS:-1}" ;;
wgpu-stats) ENVV="$WGPU_ENV TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=1" ;;
all-rust) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_RUST_RTL=all TSFP_RUST_KIO=1 TSFP_RUST_KCLOCK=1" ;;
ui-display) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_UI_DISPLAY_RATE=1"; ARGS="$ARGS --wgpu-share $MK_ARGS"; ui_overlay=1 ;;
wgpu-share) ARGS="$ARGS --wgpu-share" ;;
perf) perf=1; ENVV="$WGPU_ENV TSFP_RT_HOST_STATS=1"; ARGS="$ARGS --perf-log" ;;
kio) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_RUST_KIO=1" ;;
bisect) ports="--rust-ports=all,$blocked_roots,-$(printf '%s' "$groups" | sed 's/,/,-/g')" ;;
widescreen) ARGS="$ARGS --aspect 16:9" ;;
ui-rust-shell) ui_overlay=1 ;;
ultrawide) ARGS="$ARGS --aspect 21:9" ;;
superwide) ARGS="$ARGS --aspect 32:9" ;;
mk) ports="--rust-ports=all,player,$blocked_roots"; ARGS="$ARGS $MK_ARGS" ;;
mk-interim) ARGS="$ARGS --input-router --mouse-keyboard --no-raw-look" ;;
*) echo "play.sh: unknown variant '$variant' (see --help)" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
case $variant in
safe|fileio) ;; # explicit reduced host variants do not run the game arena
*) ENVV="${ENVV:+$ENVV }TSFP_RUST_GAME_ARENA=${TSFP_RUST_GAME_ARENA:-1}" ;;
esac
renderer_env=$(tsfp_renderer_environment "$renderer") || exit $?
[ -z "$renderer_env" ] || ENVV="${ENVV:+$ENVV }$renderer_env"
case $ports in --rust-ports=off) ;; *) [ "$lifted_effects" = 0 ] || ports="$ports,-effects" ;; esac
if [ "$unlock_all" = 1 ]; then ARGS="$ARGS --unlock-all"; fi
# T2295: the wgpu variants show the rt-host picture (CPU hand-off, T2227 readback ring); without --wgpu-live the shell
# showed the C renderer and the rt-host frame was rendered but never displayed. wgpu-share takes the GPU texture path instead.
case "$ENVV" in
*TSFP_WGPU_LIVE=1*) case " $ARGS " in *" --wgpu-share "*) ;; *) ARGS="$ARGS --wgpu-live" ;; esac ;;
esac

root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
cd "$root"
# T3745 (docs/t3745-disk-safety.md): temporary files on the data disk, never /tmp on the root
# disk, no core dumps, and the disk budget gate (tools/data/disk_budget.json) before anything is
# written. Exit 3 only on a refusal; a checkout without tools/datadisk.py skips the gate.
# No core dumps (core_pattern pipes them to the host root disk); TSFP_CORE_DUMPS=1 opts in.
[ "${TSFP_CORE_DUMPS:-0}" = 1 ] || ulimit -S -c 0 2>/dev/null || ulimit -c 0
if [ -f "$root/tools/datadisk.py" ] && command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    if tsfp_tmpdir=$(python3 -m tools.datadisk tmpdir 2>/dev/null); then
        export TMPDIR="$tsfp_tmpdir" TMP="$tsfp_tmpdir" TEMP="$tsfp_tmpdir" GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES="$tsfp_tmpdir"
        # GPU shader caches of the game on the data disk too (Mesa, NVIDIA), not in ~/.cache on the root disk
        export MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR="${MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR:-$(dirname "$tsfp_tmpdir")/cache/mesa}"
        export __GL_SHADER_DISK_CACHE_PATH="${__GL_SHADER_DISK_CACHE_PATH:-$(dirname "$tsfp_tmpdir")/cache/nvidia}"
    fi
    tsfp_disk_rc=0
    python3 -m tools.datadisk check --kind play --path "$root/tmp" || tsfp_disk_rc=$?
    [ "$tsfp_disk_rc" != 3 ] || exit 3
fi
if [ -x .venv/bin/python ]; then py=.venv/bin/python; else py=python3; fi
target_dir=${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-tmp/bevy-target}
# T2472: the shared cache lives under the MAIN checkout (git common dir parent), never a fixed container path.
if [ -z "${TSFP_PREBUILT_ROOT:-}" ]; then
    common=$(git -C "$root" rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir 2>/dev/null) || common="$root/.git"
    prebuilt_root=$(dirname "$common")/tmp/wt-cache/prebuilt
else
    prebuilt_root=$TSFP_PREBUILT_ROOT
fi
# The owner's own run is not an agent session: it reuses a cached host when one exists but never builds into the cache.
agent_session=0
if [ "${TSFP_OWNER_BUILD:-0}" != 1 ] && { [ "${TSFP_AGENT:-0}" = 1 ] || [ -n "${CLAUDECODE:-}" ] || [ -n "${CODEX_SANDBOX:-}" ]; }; then agent_session=1; fi
host=${TSFP_HOST:-}
[ "$emit_options" = 0 ] || host=emit-options-no-host
local_build() {
    if [ "$dry" = 1 ]; then host=$target_dir/release/tsfp-bevy; return 0; fi  # dry run never builds or waits
    echo "play.sh: building host locally (target=$target_dir)"
    CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$target_dir" sh tools/dev/build.sh || exit $?
    host=$target_dir/release/tsfp-bevy
}
host_why=
[ -z "$host" ] || host_why="TSFP_HOST is set"
# T3833: --capture-targets runs the live capture play host, a TSFP_BUILD_CAPTURE=1 TSFP_CAPTURE_KIND=play prebuilt (its own
# input hash, I-T3784-3). It shares the variant-aware artifact store and remote build policy.
if [ -n "$capture_targets" ]; then
    TSFP_BUILD_CAPTURE=1 TSFP_CAPTURE_KIND=play  # the prebuilt key of every lookup below (tools.wt prebuilt)
    export TSFP_BUILD_CAPTURE TSFP_CAPTURE_KIND
fi
# Existing separate-cache artifacts remain readable; new builds use the shared variant namespace.
capture_cache=${TSFP_CAPTURE_PLAY_CACHE:-$prebuilt_root}
legacy_capture_cache=$(dirname "$prebuilt_root")/prebuilt-capture-play
if [ -n "$capture_targets" ] && [ -z "$host" ] && [ "$emit_options" = 0 ]; then
    capture_commit=$(git -C "$root" rev-parse HEAD) || exit 2
    host=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt path --worktree "$root" --cache "$capture_cache" --commit "$capture_commit" --if-present 2>/dev/null) || host=
    if [ -z "$host" ] && [ -z "${TSFP_CAPTURE_PLAY_CACHE:-}" ] && [ "$legacy_capture_cache" != "$capture_cache" ]; then
        host=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt path --worktree "$root" --cache "$legacy_capture_cache" --commit "$capture_commit" --if-present 2>/dev/null) || host=
    fi
    if [ -z "$host" ] && [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
        echo "play.sh: building the capture play host (once per commit, TSFP_BUILD_CAPTURE=1 TSFP_CAPTURE_KIND=play)" >&2
        nice -n "${TSFP_CAPTURE_BUILD_NICE:-10}" python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt build --worktree "$root" --cache "$capture_cache" --commit "$capture_commit" --remote "${TSFP_PREBUILT_REMOTE:-auto}" || exit $?
        host=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt path --worktree "$root" --cache "$capture_cache" --commit "$capture_commit" 2>/dev/null) || host=
    fi
    [ -n "$host" ] || host=$capture_cache/not-built/tsfp-bevy
    host_why="capture play prebuilt (--capture-targets)"
    LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$(dirname "$host")${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"  # published libtsfp_* beside it (T2359)
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH
fi
if [ -n "$capture_targets" ] && [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
    python3 -m tools.t2capture.live_targets check-host "$host" || exit 2
fi
# Owner report 2026-10-24: build.sh records the binary it just built (it honours CARGO_TARGET_DIR), so run exactly that one.
last_build=${TSFP_LAST_BUILD:-$root/tmp/play/last-build.json}
if [ -z "$host" ] && [ -f "$last_build" ]; then
    pointed=$(sed -n 's/.*"path": *"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' "$last_build" | head -1)
    if [ -n "$pointed" ] && [ -x "$pointed" ]; then
        host=$pointed
        host_why="binary recorded by the last build.sh run ($last_build)"
    fi
fi
if [ -z "$host" ] && [ -n "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-}" ] && [ -x "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/tsfp-bevy" ]; then
    host=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/tsfp-bevy
    host_why="CARGO_TARGET_DIR is set and holds a built host"
fi
if [ -z "$host" ]; then
    # T3863: committed task changes can already have a published host. Compare
    # only uncommitted inputs, then resolve/build that exact HEAD through the
    # shared input-key cache (including docs-only aliases).
    base=$(git -C "$root" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null) || base=
    needs_build=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt needs-build --worktree "$root" --base "$base" 2>/dev/null | head -1) || needs_build=error
    if [ -n "$base" ] && [ "$needs_build" = no ]; then
        host=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt path --worktree "$root" --commit "$base" --if-present 2>/dev/null) || host=
        if [ -z "$host" ] && [ "$agent_session" = 1 ] && [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
            if python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt build --worktree "$root" --commit "$base"; then
                host=$(python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt path --worktree "$root" --commit "$base" 2>/dev/null) || host=
            else
                echo "play.sh: prebuilt build failed, falling back to a local build" >&2
            fi
        fi
        [ -n "$host" ] || local_build
    else
        [ "$needs_build" = yes ] && echo "play.sh: Rust/C host inputs changed" || echo "play.sh: prebuilt cache unavailable" >&2
        local_build
    fi
fi
[ -n "$host_why" ] || host_why="prebuilt cache or default target dir"
echo "play.sh: host $host ($host_why)" >&2
if [ "$print_host" = 1 ]; then echo "$host"; exit 0; fi
# A dry run only prints the command, so the host need not exist.
if [ "$dry" = 1 ] && [ ! -x "$host" ]; then :; else case "$host" in
    "$prebuilt_root"/*) [ -x "$host" ] && python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt run --worktree "$root" --host "$host" -- true || { echo "play.sh: invalid prebuilt host: $host" >&2; exit 2; } ;;
    *) [ -x "$host" ] || { echo "play.sh: explicit host is not executable: $host" >&2; exit 2; } ;;
esac; fi
disc=${TSFP_DISC:-$(default_disc)}
# T2189 slice 15: the shell reads these (the disc path may contain spaces, so not through ENVV).
if [ "${ui_overlay:-0}" = 1 ]; then
    # T2168: the merged tree (every captured front-end page) when present, else the single tree. T2315: optional, without a
    # tree file the shell reads every page from its live page record (no prepared tree needed).
    if [ -z "${TSFP_UI_TREE:-}" ]; then
        if [ -e tmp/ui-tree/tree-merged.json ]; then TSFP_UI_TREE=tmp/ui-tree/tree-merged.json; else TSFP_UI_TREE=tmp/ui-tree/tree.json; fi
    fi
    # T2312: native Rust HUD for the core elements (ammo rows, weapon reticle, health and armour arcs with the hit-direction flash, Arcade rank box and radar since increment 5, Story button prompt panel and Arcade effect icons since increment 6, HUD message pickup line and sliding titles since increment 7, weapon slot panel and Challenge POINTS row since increment 8); TSFP_HUD_NATIVE=off keeps the legacy HUD.
    TSFP_HUD_NATIVE=${TSFP_HUD_NATIVE:-core}
    export TSFP_UI=rust TSFP_UI_DISC="$disc" TSFP_UI_TREE TSFP_HUD_NATIVE
    [ "$dry" = 1 ] && echo "TSFP_UI=rust TSFP_UI_DISC='$disc' TSFP_UI_TREE=$TSFP_UI_TREE TSFP_HUD_NATIVE=$TSFP_HUD_NATIVE"
fi
stamp=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
rundir=tmp/play/$variant-$stamp
perf_err=tmp/perf-$variant-$stamp.err
if [ "$record" = 1 ] || [ -n "$replay" ]; then
    # Native Rust input capture is independent of the selected renderer and is off for normal play.
    case " $ARGS " in *" --input-router "*) ;; *) ARGS="$ARGS $MK_ARGS" ;; esac
    if [ "$record" = 1 ]; then
        ARGS="$ARGS --input-record $rundir/input.rec"
    else
        ARGS="$ARGS --input-replay $replay"
    fi
    case " $ENVV " in *" TSFP_SIMULATION_PACE="*) ;; *) ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_SIMULATION_PACE=1" ;; esac
    if [ "$record" = 1 ]; then echo "input recording: native Rust router; F12 adds a mark"; else echo "input replay: native Rust router from $replay"; fi
fi
# T3592: the single source of the play.sh host options. tools.rust_trace.play_options reads this JSON so a capture,
# a gate and a replay queue job run the options of a live `play.sh [variant]`, never a copy that drifts.
if [ "$emit_options" = 1 ]; then
    # shellcheck disable=SC2086
    set -- $ENVV
    TSFP_EMIT_ENV="$*" TSFP_EMIT_PORTS="$ports" TSFP_EMIT_ARGS="$ARGS" TSFP_EMIT_BASE="$BASE" \
        python3 -c 'import json,os;e={k:v for k,v in (w.split("=",1) for w in os.environ["TSFP_EMIT_ENV"].split())}
for k in ("TSFP_UI","TSFP_UI_DISC","TSFP_UI_TREE","TSFP_HUD_NATIVE"):
    if k in os.environ: e[k]=os.environ[k]
print(json.dumps({"env":e,"ports":os.environ["TSFP_EMIT_PORTS"],"args":os.environ["TSFP_EMIT_ARGS"].split(),"base":os.environ["TSFP_EMIT_BASE"].split()},sort_keys=True))'
    exit 0
fi
if [ "$replay_hold" = 1 ]; then
    ENVV="$ENVV TSFP_INPUT_REPLAY_HOLD=1"
    echo "input replay: neutral input continues after the recorded route ends"
fi

if [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
    [ -x "$host" ] || { echo "play.sh: no host binary at $host, run: sh tools/dev/build.sh" >&2; exit 3; }
    [ -e "$disc" ] || { echo "play.sh: no disc image at '$disc', put your disc there or set TSFP_DISC" >&2; exit 4; }
fi

# T2150: refuse to run a binary built from other sources than the checkout (the stamp is written by build.sh).
stamp_file=${TSFP_BUILD_STAMP:-$(dirname "$host")/.tsfp-build-stamp}
if [ ! -f "$stamp_file" ]; then
    echo "play.sh: WARNING: no build stamp at $stamp_file, cannot tell whether the binary matches the checkout." >&2
    echo "         Rebuild with: sh tools/dev/build.sh" >&2
else
    read -r built_sha built_fp built_lift_key < "$stamp_file" || true
    read -r now_sha now_fp now_lift_key <<STAMP
$(sh tools/dev/stamp.sh)
STAMP
    if [ -z "${built_lift_key:-}" ]; then
        echo "play.sh: note: the build stamp has no lift key (built before T2248), rebuild to enable the stale-lift check." >&2
    elif [ "$built_lift_key" != "$now_lift_key" ]; then
        echo "lift is STALE vs seeds/lifter (key $built_lift_key != $now_lift_key): run sh tools/dev/build.sh --relift" >&2
        exit 10
    fi
    if [ "${built_fp:-}" != "$now_fp" ]; then
        files=$(git diff --name-only "${built_sha:-HEAD}" HEAD -- src crates cmake CMakeLists.txt tools/build_bevy.sh 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
        commits=$(git rev-list --count "${built_sha:-HEAD}..HEAD" 2>/dev/null || echo "?")
        echo "play.sh: ################################################################" >&2
        echo "play.sh: binary is STALE: built at $(printf %.9s "${built_sha:-unknown}"), checkout is $(printf %.9s "$now_sha"); run sh tools/dev/build.sh" >&2
        echo "play.sh: $commits commits and $files files under src/ crates/ cmake/ changed since the build" >&2
        echo "play.sh: ################################################################" >&2
        if [ "$allow_stale" = 1 ]; then
            echo "play.sh: continuing anyway (--allow-stale / TSFP_ALLOW_STALE=1)" >&2
        else
            echo "play.sh: refusing to run; pass --allow-stale to override" >&2
            exit 6
        fi
    fi
fi

# T2359: published hosts carry every libtsfp runtime beside the binary. Prefer
# this immutable bundle over absolute RUNPATHs left by the build worktree.
main_root=$(cd "$root" && cd "$(dirname "$(git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir)")" && pwd)
case "$host" in
    "$prebuilt_root"/*)
        if [ -n "${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}" ]; then
            LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$(dirname "$host"):$LD_LIBRARY_PATH"
        else
            LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$(dirname "$host")
        fi
        export LD_LIBRARY_PATH
        ;;
esac

# T2233: the host links libtsfp_*_capi.so / libtsfp_rt_host.so through an absolute build-time RUNPATH. A moved checkout (or a binary
# built on another machine) then exits 127 before any window exists. Look for the libraries under tmp/*/rust-*/release, else say how to fix.
if [ "$dry" = 0 ] && command -v ldd >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    missing=$(ldd "$host" 2>&1 | sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*\(lib[^ ]*\) => not found.*/\1/p' | tr '\n' ' ')
    # A build running in this tree rewrites the libraries for a moment: wait a few seconds before judging.
    waited=0
    while [ -n "$missing" ] && [ "$waited" -lt "${TSFP_LIB_WAIT:-8}" ]; do
        [ "$waited" != 0 ] || echo "play.sh: libraries missing ($missing), another process may be rebuilding them; waiting up to ${TSFP_LIB_WAIT:-8} s" >&2
        sleep 1
        waited=$((waited + 1))
        missing=$(ldd "$host" 2>&1 | sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*\(lib[^ ]*\) => not found.*/\1/p' | tr '\n' ' ')
    done
    if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
        found=""
        for libdir in $(ls -dt tmp/*/rust-*/release 2>/dev/null); do
            found="$found:$libdir"
        done
        if [ -n "$found" ]; then
            LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${found#:}${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}
            export LD_LIBRARY_PATH
            missing=$(ldd "$host" 2>&1 | sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*\(lib[^ ]*\) => not found.*/\1/p' | tr '\n' ' ')
        fi
        if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
            echo "play.sh: the host cannot start, missing libraries: $missing" >&2
            echo "         the binary was built in another place or on another machine; rebuild here: sh tools/dev/build.sh --reconfigure" >&2
            exit 7
        fi
        echo "play.sh: libraries found through LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH (the build RUNPATH points elsewhere)" >&2
    fi
fi

# T2146: adapter policy of the wgpu variants. The live path must use the real GPU (RADV on the owner host).
# play.sh never sets VK_ICD_FILENAMES or TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER itself, so the Vulkan loader sees every installed ICD
# and the rt-host prefers the best real adapter (llvmpipe/lavapipe only when no GPU exists). Your own
# VK_ICD_FILENAMES / TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER (a name part, an index or "software") still win. The banner
# "wgpu-live: rt-host adapter ..." is echoed below and kept in $rundir/host.err.
adapter_policy=""
case "$ENVV" in
*TSFP_WGPU_LIVE=1*)
    case " $ARGS " in *" --wgpu-share "*) shared_gpu=1 ;; *) shared_gpu=0 ;; esac
    if [ "$shared_gpu" = 1 ]; then adapter_policy="the shell opens the shared device itself: discrete GPU first, WGPU_ADAPTER_NAME=<part of a name> picks another (TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER is not used); the 'tsfp-bevy: --wgpu-share: path=' line names the adapter or the reason for the CPU fallback"
    elif [ -n "${TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER:-}" ]; then adapter_policy="adapter forced by your TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER=$TSFP_WGPU_ADAPTER"
    elif [ -n "${VK_ICD_FILENAMES:-}" ]; then adapter_policy="Vulkan ICDs forced by your VK_ICD_FILENAMES=$VK_ICD_FILENAMES"
    else adapter_policy="best real adapter (RADV/NVIDIA/Intel), software only as last resort"; fi ;;
esac

# T3824: a live hit census build (TSFP_BUILD_LIVE_CENSUS, see build.sh) writes which lifted functions ran to
# $rundir/census-hits.bin; the build stamp names the exact build. Other builds ignore these variables. Exported, not
# part of the shown command (it names the run dir).
if [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
    TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_OUT=${TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_OUT:-$rundir/census-hits.bin}
    TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_BUILD=${TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_BUILD:-${built_sha:-}}
    TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_LIFT=${TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_LIFT:-${built_lift_key:-}}
    export TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_OUT TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_BUILD TSFP_LIVE_CENSUS_LIFT
fi
# T3833: --capture-targets: the ALLOW list and budget seed of this run, the spool $rundir/capture.bin and its live
# provenance (run id, build sha, port set), exported for the capture host (tools.t2capture.live_targets prepare).
if [ -n "$capture_targets" ] && [ "$dry" = 0 ]; then
    capture_env=$(python3 -m tools.t2capture.live_targets prepare --run-dir "$rundir" --targets "$capture_targets" --build-sha "${built_sha:-}" --ports="$ports") || exit 2
    eval "$capture_env"
fi
# Print the command with quoting, relative paths only.
show="${ENVV:+$ENVV }$py -m tools.play --host $host --disc '$disc' $BASE $ports ${ARGS:+$ARGS }$play_timeout --run-dir $rundir${extra:+ $extra}"
[ "$perf" = 0 ] || show="$show 2> $perf_err"
echo "variant: $variant"
echo "run dir: $rundir"
echo "command: $show"
if [ "${ui_overlay:-0}" = 1 ]; then
    echo "keys: in the menus main menu: mouse hover/click, right click or Esc = Back, arrows/Enter; F9 = original menu input; in game Esc = pause menu (Start); Alt+F4 or the window close button quits"
else
    echo "keys: Esc = pause menu (Start), Alt+F4 or the window close button quits (Esc no longer quits)"
fi
[ -z "$adapter_policy" ] || echo "adapter policy: $adapter_policy (look for the 'wgpu-live: rt-host adapter' line below)"
[ "$dry" = 0 ] || exit 0

mkdir -p tmp/play
start=$(date +%s)
rc=0
# shellcheck disable=SC2086
if [ "$perf" = 1 ]; then
    case "$host" in
        "$prebuilt_root"/*) python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt run --worktree "$root" --host "$host" -- env $ENVV "$py" -m tools.play --host "$host" --disc "$disc" $BASE $ports $ARGS $play_timeout --run-dir "$rundir" $extra 2> "$perf_err" || rc=$? ;;
        *) env $ENVV "$py" -m tools.play --host "$host" --disc "$disc" $BASE $ports $ARGS $play_timeout --run-dir "$rundir" $extra 2> "$perf_err" || rc=$? ;;
    esac
else
    case "$host" in
        "$prebuilt_root"/*) python3 -m tools.wt prebuilt run --worktree "$root" --host "$host" -- env $ENVV "$py" -m tools.play --host "$host" --disc "$disc" $BASE $ports $ARGS $play_timeout --run-dir "$rundir" $extra || rc=$? ;;
        *) env $ENVV "$py" -m tools.play --host "$host" --disc "$disc" $BASE $ports $ARGS $play_timeout --run-dir "$rundir" $extra || rc=$? ;;
    esac
fi
elapsed=$(( $(date +%s) - start ))
# T3824: keep the live hit census beyond the run dir (durable store tmp/live-census, tools.live_census).
if [ -f "$rundir/census-hits.bin" ]; then
    python3 -m tools.live_census persist "$rundir" || echo "play.sh: live census: persist failed, $rundir/census-hits.bin kept" >&2
fi
# T3833: ingest the live capture into tmp/t2corpus-f2 (t2-continuous picks the changed entry sets up).
if [ -n "$capture_targets" ]; then
    python3 -m tools.t2capture.live_targets ingest --run-dir "$rundir" || echo "play.sh: capture targets: ingest failed, $rundir/capture.bin kept (retry: python3 -m tools.t2capture.live_targets ingest --run-dir $rundir)" >&2
fi

echo
echo "== run finished (exit $rc, ${elapsed}s) =="
census=$(grep -rh '^CALL CENSUS' "$rundir" 2>/dev/null | head -1 || true)
if [ -n "$census" ]; then
    echo "$census"
    total=$(printf '%s' "$census" | sed -n 's/^CALL CENSUS *\([0-9][0-9]*\) total.*/\1/p')
    if [ -n "$total" ] && [ "$elapsed" -gt 0 ]; then
        echo "calls/s (total / wall seconds, includes start-up): $((total / elapsed))"
    fi
else
    echo "CALL CENSUS: not found in $rundir"
fi
if [ "$perf" = 1 ]; then
    cat <<SEND
Send back: $perf_err (the 'perf t=' and 'perf bevy t=' lines), the CALL CENSUS line and calls/s above,
the first 40 'perf roots' rows and the 'guest frame trace (T1289)' lines of $rundir/host.out, and 'nproc'.
SEND
fi
exit "$rc"

